{
  "case_id": "2024-24-249",
  "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "NICOLE F. REAVES, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "The district has conceded Ava's question presented. Both sides now agree that the ADA and the Rehabilitation Act apply the same legal standards to all plaintiffs and that it's wrong to impose any sort of uniquely stringent test on children facing discrimination at school. That concession fully resolves this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Now they say that the statutes apply a bad-faith or gross-misjudgment test to all plaintiffs, not just schoolchildren protected by the IDEA. That's exactly the opposite of what they told you at the cert stage, where they said that no bad faith or intent is required outside the IDEA context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Isn't there an argument, though, that we should -- that some would think is embedded or included in the question presented, and that is what is the standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: If --if we do what you say and say that there's no unique standard in the schools context, it'll still be open to the court on remand to decide which standard is appropriate throughout, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Point taken on that. And then what -- can you explain the delta between, on the one hand, \"deliberate indifference\" at least as the Solicitor General defines it and \"bad faith\" or \"gross misjudgment\" on the other hand? Because the way they define \"deliberate indifference\" sounds a lot like someone acting in bad faith."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "it requires motive, which, in their brief, they describe in various places as requiring a sinister state of mind or something, you know, approximating a bare desire to harm. And so I think that's an animus-type test that requires more than the knowledge that there's a substantial likelihood of a violation --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm not sure where any of these tests come from, because mens rea is generally willfulness, which requires knowing what the law is, but the statute doesn't talk about willfulness. Motive, in -- intent -- we don't care about motive. We've said that repeatedly in a bunch of different contexts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Mr. Martinez, has any other circuit taken the view or is this argument that the other side is pressing, is that one that's kind of a live issue in the lower courts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Martinez",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. MARTINEZ: I -- I would doubt that because of the fact that the reason these five courts have applied this Monahan test is really because, and as they explained it very well in their brief in opposition, it's all about the IDEA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: -- do you agree with the SG's formulation of deliberate indifference? Any problems with how they formulate it in their brief?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0001-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MS. REAVES: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: There is no sound basis for applying different intent requirements to Title II and Section 504 claims brought in the school context. The texts of those provisions apply to qualified individuals and provide relief to any person and do not distinguish among different contexts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you think was the impulse that led so many lower courts to adopt the standard that you find to be completely unsupported?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. REAVES",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there was enough to go to trial because there was deliberate indifference because these individuals had repeatedly requested an interpreter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. REAVES",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Monahan, the Eighth Circuit laid out, which was this desire to harmonize the IDEA with the -- with Section 504 and Title II."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, don't these two statutes proceed a -- along very different lines? Under the IDEA, the school district must provide a free appropriate public education. That can be extremely expensive, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Reaves, if we decide that this dual-track approach is incorrect and if we say nothing about the appropriate standards with respect to either damages or injunctions, what's your understanding of what could properly happen below?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You said that clear notice was important, I think, in this context in damages claims. And the other side says that your framing of deliberate indifference, in particular, actual knowledge that a federally protected right was substantially likely to be violated -- they focus on substantially likely --that that does not give in this context school districts clear notice of what they have to do, particular -- you know, something like this, 4:30 p.m. or 6 p.m., and that it's therefore -- and you're talking about reasonable accommodations and line drawing to Justice Alito's question. How do we deal with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "This Court should affirm Monahan. Bare IDEA violations do not support liability under Section 504 or the ADA. Instead, the defendant must have acted with discriminatory intent. Monahan correctly described that intent as bad faith, which is the longstanding term for actions done for an improper reason, here, disability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "intent requirement for liability and injunctions. That's wrong. When Congress wanted intent-free liability, it said so expressly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You -- you believe that Mr. Martinez and the Solicitor General are lying? Is that your accusation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice JACKSON",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, Ms. Blatt, you -- in order to say it's uniquely stupid, I think you would have to point to at least one other circuit that has actually applied the bad-faith standard in a different context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Our definition of \"bad faith\" is discriminatory intent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BARRETT",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And that would be a sea change, right? That's what the other side told us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Judge Sutton's opinion in the Sixth Circuit, and that counts as a court, has held that --that this statute, just like Title IX and Title VI, requires discriminatory intent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On the -- on the level down/level up point, you're defining \"bad faith\" so it doesn't require animus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice JACKSON",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It did not say decide the standard. I'm reading. The question presented is whether the ADA and Rehabilitation Act require children with disabilities to satisfy a uniquely stringent bad-faith-or-gross- misjudgment standard when seeking relief for discrimination relating to their education."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "But, Justice Jackson, there's no disagreement that we've always said that there is a big problem with the other side's argument in the school context, because every IDEA disagreement now risks the loss of federal funding and injunctive relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But nowhere else have I seen the use of deliberate indifference or gross enough indifference used to define intentional discrimination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: By the way, intent's not even an issue here because there wasn't an injunction being -- or the lack of an injunction challenged here. They got the injunction under the IDEA, didn't they?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "the blue brief said that there is no intent required."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Deliberate indifference is not an intent standard"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 97,
        "start": 97
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: I don't know how you can know that a federally protected right was substantially likely to be violated without having some idea what the law provides."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-249",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9ff217544eaa-0004-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 105,
        "start": 105
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
